{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation","id":1082476,"title":"Destroying the Garou Nation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-22T18:48:00-07:00","id":1082476,"title":"Destroying the Garou Nation","content":"In the thread for the 5th Edition, one of the controversial items is the split in the Garou Nation down the lines of 'Traditional' vs 'Modern', and the way the divide fell between the Tribes.<br /> <br /> However, it occurred to me that some divisions already exist. Obviously, the Uktena and Wendigo haven't been happy with the way things have gone since Columbus arrived. The Shadow Lords are split into a seperate sub-tribe divided by their home range (East of the Carpathians to the Pacific Ocean are Haken). Baba Yaga's curtain causing yet another split, as the Tribes in Russia found them selves cut off from their main people, which would have put huge pressure on the Silver Fangs. The Amazon war found itself a Get of Fenris that discarded the typical stance on working with Bastet and Mokole, and the various Garou in Africa had to actually take a subservient role to the Simba and Ajaba over the course of two tyrants reigns and the building of the Ahadi. (And the Red Talons had to also put themselves beneath the Mokole) And don't forget the Stargazers ping ponging pack and forth. (As if they had the numbers to matter.)<br /> <br /> So what if the concept of a 'Garou Nation' simply couldn't hold up under the fractitious strain and it simply ceased to be?<br /> <br /> Instead of one, overriding voice in the world, more focus on local politics of the Tribes and how they get along?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T21:01:05-07:00","id":1082506,"title":"","content":"Extinction of all life as the Wyrm or Weaver overwhelms the last defenders of Gaia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T23:15:03-07:00","id":1082526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1082506#post1082506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extinction of all life as the Wyrm or Weaver overwhelms the last defenders of Gaia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, I'm not saying there would be any fewer Garou. More like the same split we already see with the Beast Courts (Haken) and the Ahadi (Red Talons) <br /> <br /> Rather than, as BNS uses, a tribal basis for the split, it instead becomes a geographic one, where the Garou of North Armerica, North Asia, Europe, and the Middle East no longer understand each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T06:35:56-07:00","id":1082578,"title":"","content":"Yes, without the organization of the Garou Nation, everything outside of East Asia and Sub-Saharan Africa starts to fragment. While the Garou Nation has its flaws, it does allow some measure of mutual defense between Tribes. Without that, the Wyrm and the Weaver can just pick off the Garou Tribes one at a time. Now, if the Garou Nation is replaced by a Fera organization like the Beast Courts, that is another thing entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:36:17-07:00","id":1082603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1082526#post1082526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind, I'm not saying there would be any fewer Garou. More like the same split we already see with the Beast Courts (Haken) and the Ahadi (Red Talons) <br /> <br /> Rather than, as BNS uses, a tribal basis for the split, it instead becomes a geographic one, where the Garou of North Armerica, North Asia, Europe, and the Middle East no longer understand each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>This always felt like the eventuality of WtA to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:38:33-07:00","id":1082605,"title":"","content":"If we look at it from a historic perspective, think about the Nation as Britain. When they started out to conquer new lands they managed to take Canada, the United States, South Africa, and Australia among other smaller grabs here and there. Eventually one those factions broke away from the first and in time the others did as well. Sure, they are all still allies but each primarily focuses on it corner of the world and their are always political barriers that need to be hurdled. <br /> <br /> So, I have to agree with Aya to some degree. Right now the garou tribes may not like one another and their is internal strife but they are united under a common doctrine which guides them in their corner of the WoD. If you were to start breaking them up the way you are proposing then the most likely result is that the geographic coalitions would start to segregate themselves further. This separation of leadership would cause power struggles for the Wyrm to wiggle into and eventually it would start pitting faction against faction.<br /> <br /> From a storytelling stand point this would be a nightmare. Right now you only need to deal with cultural differences on a tribal scale. If you were to throw in Factional cultural differences on top of that you would have to plan out all of your chronicles very differently. The Ahadi and the Courts are great but when outsiders come in they are at a disadvantage and a good part of it is mechanics like the way rank is handled in these places is different so if you want to gain rank you have to start over and each faction also has additional pools of gifts that aren't shared with outsiders.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:13:57-07:00","id":1082619,"title":"","content":"glad your not someone who thinks pentex is the good guys.<br /> yes that was my first thought, and wont lie, the idea filled me with outrage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-23-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T11:28:44-07:00","id":1082720,"title":"","content":"I never did understand why anyone would think that Pentex is a good guy. The opposite of capitalistic behavior is monopolistic behavior (read Wealth of Nations if you do not believe me) and Pentex is very much a monopolistic corporation (like most large corporations). If people believe in anarchism, capitalism, communism, socialism, or basically anything but fascism, they should consider Pentex to be the bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:10:01-07:00","id":1082748,"title":"","content":"Plus, you know, Pentex literally wants to destroy the world and slowly kill everyone with horrific toxins. Kind of hard to imagine anyone who would think they're the good guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:44:39-07:00","id":1082800,"title":"","content":"Some... people still think that kinnd of thing.<br /> <br /> A bitch from AOL I knew thought that anything &quot;Labeling&quot; them bad guys should be removed,<br /> <br /> because she thought the potential for moral dillemna's with the fact Pentex was arguably justified under the laws of war, killing a garou cub before their fisting was interesting<br /> <br /> and was incensed that kind of thing was impossible as pentex didnt give a fuck about the laws and conventions of war in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T22:49:13-07:00","id":1082907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1082720#post1082720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never did understand why anyone would think that Pentex is a good guy. The opposite of capitalistic behavior is monopolistic behavior (read Wealth of Nations if you do not believe me) and Pentex is very much a monopolistic corporation (like most large corporations). If people believe in anarchism, capitalism, communism, socialism, or basically anything but fascism, they should consider Pentex to be the bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascists wouldn't like Pentex either. Basically, you have to be the Wyrm to like Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T22:55:16-07:00","id":1082908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1082907#post1082907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fascists wouldn't like Pentex either. Basically, you have to be the Wyrm to like Pentex.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that, but just about everyone who isn't aware of the concept of spiritual corrosion is willing to play ball to get something that they want from them, and even some who are still end up hoodwinked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T00:34:47-07:00","id":1082929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1082800#post1082800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some... people still think that kinnd of thing.<br /> <br /> A bitch from AOL I knew thought that anything &quot;Labeling&quot; them bad guys should be removed,<br /> <br /> because she thought the potential for moral dillemna's with the fact Pentex was arguably justified under the laws of war, killing a garou cub before their fisting was interesting<br /> <br /> and was incensed that kind of thing was impossible as pentex didnt give a fuck about the laws and conventions of war in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bRegardless of that person's stance on Pentex could you please not use the word &quot;bitch&quot; to describe a female you disagree with? You can certainly make the point that some people think the way she does about Pentex without prefacing it with a seemingly sexist and dismissive statement.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T04:57:21-07:00","id":1082972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1082929#post1082929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bRegardless of that person's stance on Pentex could you please not use the word &quot;bitch&quot; to describe a female you disagree with? You can certainly make the point that some people think the way she does about Pentex without prefacing it with a seemingly sexist and dismissive statement.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>sorry, just really hated her, not just for that.<br /> <br /> But your right, it was out of line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:31:33-07:00","id":1083051,"title":"","content":"Well, not many people who aren't totally Wyrm corrupted know the end game of Pentex. They might know that they are up to no good and so are willing to play ball for the right price, but many might change their minds if they knew what players know from reading the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1082972#post1082972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sorry, just really hated her, not just for that.<br /> <br /> But your right, it was out of line.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Pentex are designed to totally evil villains, and so it's hard to argue in favor of them, I wouldn't have too much hostility for somebody because of their opinions about some fictional organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 04-24-2017, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:31:55-07:00","id":1083161,"title":"","content":"had many many many many other reasons for my antaganism that was just a reason that came up.<br /> <br /> thing is she KNEW that, but thought it was wrong... thinking that it wasted a perfectly good opportunity to have a &quot;dialague&quot; on environmentalism, but I wasnt <i>interested</i>, in 'fairplay' to the other side","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:20:32-07:00","id":1083436,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that most people who play WtA are at least somewhat sympathetic to environmental argument because they understand that their quality of life degrades as the environment degrades (look at the air quality of Beijing or New Delhi if you want to see what few enforced environmental laws result in).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T23:11:29-07:00","id":1087532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1082800#post1082800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some... people still think that kinnd of thing.<br /> <br /> A bitch from AOL I knew thought that anything &quot;Labeling&quot; them bad guys should be removed,<br /> <br /> because she thought the potential for moral dillemna's with the fact Pentex was arguably justified under the laws of war, killing a garou cub before their fisting was interesting<br /> <br /> and was incensed that kind of thing was impossible as pentex didnt give a fuck about the laws and conventions of war in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I read Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and inferred all this wonderful irony and ambiguity, and noticed that the creation story was suspiciously simplistic, and that the Black Spiral Dancers' perspective is never given, and that their success doesn't make sense if they are as described.<br /> <br /> I assumed that like Vampire, this was a game about monsters, and I was supposed to take them with a grain of salt for that reason. I assumed that the appeal of playing rage-fueled religious fanatics was finding out what they were missing and how horribly wrong they were.<br /> <br /> And now I'm finally coming to terms with the fact that that probably wasn't the authors' intention, and most fans react violently to the idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a difference between people who just read the books and people who get around to playing the games. If you spend a lot of time inhabiting the mind of a werewolf, it must feel like a bait-and-switch for the ST to tell you your character is wrong for reasons you didn't expect.<br /> <br /> So apparently, most people just play it as a one-sided political revenge fantasy. This saddens me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5553,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","user":"Mr. Sluagh","date":". 05-04-2017, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T23:22:16-07:00","id":1087534,"title":"","content":"We actually do get to see the BSD perspective in a few books, and the frightening thing about it is they aren't necessarily <i>completely</i> wrong. If the Wyrm wasn't totally fucked, they might even be on the right side. Unfortunately, it is, so rather than what their doctrine is - 'we will unchain the wyrm and restore balance, p.s. let's go fuck in a pit of nuclear radiation because this is the 90s and we're Edgy As Fuck' - the goal they're working toward is more 'universal enslavement to malevolence and suffering'.<br /> <br /> As for labelling Pentex bad guys, well, that one is pretty unambiguous. Pentex <i>are</i> bad guys, and they would be whether or not they served the Wyrm. Their entire market model is 'maximize human suffering', and not for a 'noble' purpose like 'human suffering purifies the soul' or 'suffering breaks the chains placed on us by the demiurge', but purely for 'it will make <i>us</i>, on the individual level, wealthier/happier/immortal/whatever-we-want, even if it makes the greater collective live in wretched misery'. The greedy, malevolent corporation that literally plans to enslave the totality of existence for its own benefit is evil in a way even the Dancers aren't. There's really no moral dilemma there - there might be on the individual employee level (Jim, the plant manager who unknowingly oversaw the introduction of tainted (just chemically, not with Banes) ingredients in baby formula - just for a random example - is not necessarily a bad person or an evil one. Killing him <i>is</i> a moral dilemma) but not on the corporate totality level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T02:17:25-07:00","id":1087582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1087532#post1087532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently, most people just play it as a one-sided political revenge fantasy. This saddens me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also play it as a political exploration of Faith, principle, a clash of conservative and modern thinking and an insane trippy trip through the interplay of spirits, Fera and men. Fixating on the Captain Planet thing never does anything good for Werewolf, especially as it's not the point.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T06:51:24-07:00","id":1087652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1087532#post1087532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I read Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and inferred all this wonderful irony and ambiguity, and noticed that the creation story was suspiciously simplistic, and that the Black Spiral Dancers' perspective is never given, and that their success doesn't make sense if they are as described.<br /> <br /> I assumed that like Vampire, this was a game about monsters, and I was supposed to take them with a grain of salt for that reason. I assumed that the appeal of playing rage-fueled religious fanatics was finding out what they were missing and how horribly wrong they were.<br /> <br /> And now I'm finally coming to terms with the fact that that probably wasn't the authors' intention, and most fans react violently to the idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a difference between people who just read the books and people who get around to playing the games. If you spend a lot of time inhabiting the mind of a werewolf, it must feel like a bait-and-switch for the ST to tell you your character is wrong for reasons you didn't expect.<br /> <br /> So apparently, most people just play it as a one-sided political revenge fantasy. This saddens me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the most apparent and easiest way to play it, especially given how on-the-nose Second Edition was with its preaching.<br /> We can see the gameline as a whole really distancing itself from that stance for a different look at how Garou could and maybe shoiuld be played in Revised, especially in the Tribebooks, with their many moments of &quot;Wait the Garou DO WHAT?&quot;<br /> <br /> Nevertheless a well-conducted exploration of what playing a rage-fueled zealous monster means should not mean that you can't identify the clearly bad, well worse, guys. Black Spiral Dancers will rape, kill and eat you if htey can't make a convert out of you, often not in that order. Pentex will do the stuff loomer pointed out in their post. Banes will spread corruption and suffering so they cna feed on it, become more powerful and spread more corruption and suffering to feed even more.<br /> <br /> The only thing that could be said is that in the very long run the Wyrm's endgame might result in a good ending, depending if it results in it becoming whole again. Maybe it just needs to destroy the whole universe and have the Wyld and Weaver restart from scratch to fix things up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:40:50-07:00","id":1087678,"title":"","content":"Can packs or septs of the 2 factions work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:28:57-07:00","id":1087712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1087532#post1087532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I read Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and inferred all this wonderful irony and ambiguity, and noticed that the creation story was suspiciously simplistic, and that the Black Spiral Dancers' perspective is never given, and that their success doesn't make sense if they are as described.<br /> <br /> I assumed that like Vampire, this was a game about monsters, and I was supposed to take them with a grain of salt for that reason. I assumed that the appeal of playing rage-fueled religious fanatics was finding out what they were missing and how horribly wrong they were.<br /> <br /> And now I'm finally coming to terms with the fact that that probably wasn't the authors' intention, and most fans react <u>violently </u>to the idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a difference between people who just read the books and people who get around to playing the games. If you spend a lot of time inhabiting the mind of a werewolf, it must feel like a bait-and-switch for the ST to tell you your character is wrong for reasons you didn't expect.<br /> <br /> So apparently, most people just play it as a one-sided political revenge fantasy. This saddens me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Minor Clarification, unless their physically attacking you, you should use the word vehemently, or angrily, not violently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-04-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T09:07:22-07:00","id":1087742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1087532#post1087532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I read Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and inferred all this wonderful irony and ambiguity, and noticed that the creation story was suspiciously simplistic</div> </div> </div> </div>What's suspicious about it? In the same breath that one of the Garou or Fera realizes what they are, they also realize that the cosmos is dying. Then the Garou meets other Garou and finds out that their side is to blame for an awful lot of this shit, and they have mountains and valleys and oceans of work ahead if they're going to make anything right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I assumed that like Vampire, this was a game about monsters, and I was supposed to take them with a grain of salt for that reason. I assumed that the appeal of playing rage-fueled religious fanatics was finding out what they were missing and how horribly wrong they were. </div> </div> </div>It's not really a religion to them. It wouldn't be to humans, either, if they could see and freely communicate with spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And now I'm finally coming to terms with the fact that that probably wasn't the authors' intention, and most fans react violently to the idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a difference between people who just read the books and people who get around to playing the games. If you spend a lot of time inhabiting the mind of a werewolf, it must feel like a bait-and-switch for the ST to tell you your character is wrong for reasons you didn't expect.<br /> <br /> So apparently, most people just play it as a one-sided political revenge fantasy. This saddens me. </div> </div> </div>The game is actually quite upfront about where Garou are wrong. It's their backstory. You can either blind yourself to this and just collect accolades in old-fashioned battles, or adjust your worldview and get things done, possibly in a way that your society won't recognize or celebrate nearly as much as the traditional guy who just gets into bloody fights all the time and frequently goes Leeroy Jenkins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T18:22:42-07:00","id":1088031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1087582#post1087582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also play it as a political exploration of Faith, principle, a clash of conservative and modern thinking and an insane trippy trip through the interplay of spirits, Fera and men. Fixating on the Captain Planet thing never does anything good for Werewolf, especially as it's not the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so maybe this is on some level a conservative/liberal difference in readings? Because the &quot;Captain Planet&quot; thing was always the part I most sympathized with. It's impossible not to cherry-pick from canon, but over the years, a certain way of cherry-picking has become fan dogma.<br /> <br /> It's just that I haven't been able to enjoy the playstyles you mentioned when I'm expected to take all of the ridiculous sounding propaganda and superstition at face value for no good reason. &quot;Spiritually sterile&quot;? What does that even mean? Because all it sounds like is that there are religious taboos against circumventing metis sterility because it's a &quot;curse from Gaia&quot;, comparable to archaic Christian taboos against using medication to treat birthing pains. So not a lot of Garou have tried or reported the results. Except the Black Spiral Dancers, but everyone in the Garou Nation is prone to assuming those are all hideous Rosemary's babies of some kind. Not that they've ever, you know, met one, because eww. The First Litany and the rhetoric surrounding it sound too much like IRL homophobia for me to not want to explore that allegory.<br /> <br /> I know, I know, &quot;it's not like homosexuality, it's like incest&quot;. Except it's not quite directly analogous to either, and simplistic comparisons to incest are another common trope of anti-gay rhetoric. The incest comparison also seems like the pot calling the kettle a pervert, when it's coming from people who are as obsessed as the Garou are with breeding only with their kin for the sake of &quot;purity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Where I find the analogy between incest taboos and the first litany really collapses, though, is that most modern nations are not being torn apart by their incest taboos the way the Garou Nation is currently being torn apart by the First Litany. &quot;Think of the poor, deformed metis babies!&quot; and &quot;Love the metis, hate the parents!&quot; seem like sensible enough attitudes on the surface, and have more or less been adopted by most tribes. But if the Black Spiral Dancers' recruitment numbers are any indication, a whole lot of those &quot;pitiable, misbegotten creatures&quot; would much rather keep their deformities and not have their parents treated like shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1087534#post1087534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We actually do get to see the BSD perspective in a few books, and the frightening thing about it is they aren't necessarily <i>completely</i> wrong. If the Wyrm wasn't totally fucked, they might even be on the right side. Unfortunately, it is, so rather than what their doctrine is - 'we will unchain the wyrm and restore balance, p.s. let's go fuck in a pit of nuclear radiation because this is the 90s and we're Edgy As Fuck' - the goal they're working toward is more 'universal enslavement to malevolence and suffering'.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I keep asking simple questions like:<br /> <br /> How can the Black Spiral Dancers, as described, function as a tribe?<br /> <br /> Why would anyone, in or out of their right mind, join the Black Spiral Dancers?<br /> <br /> How have the Black Spiral Dancers been able to not only continue existing, but become the biggest and fastest-growing tribe, in spite of being universally and relentlessly violent and nihilistic?<br /> <br /> But instead of answers, all I can find are what look like randomly selected passages from something H. R. Giger wrote when he was going through puberty. That's just bad storytelling. I can't find the verisimilitude in it. One could make an analogy to ISIL or something, but even ISIL has more coherent ideals and motivations than the Black Spiral Dancers. ISIL is also much smaller than many Muslim sects, whereas the Black Spiral Dancers are somehow the largest Garou tribe, and I don't think it's overly optimistic to say ISIL doesn't have much staying power. The Black Spiral Dancers have been around longer than Islam, IIRC. Groups like that have more going for them than orgies on speed.<br /> <br /> What I think makes more sense is to suppose that what we see of the Black Spiral Dancers is how the Garou Nation sees them, and how the Garou Nation sees them is similar to what people in countries with sharia law must envision when they hear about things like &quot;rape culture on American college campuses&quot;. The Garou Nation has such a reactionary and dogmatic view of sexuality that they can't picture a tribe that doesn't accept the First Litany as anything but a nonstop rape orgy. If one doesn't understand the social context, one pictures ritualistic gang rape, but the reality is usually a lot more mundane.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Garou are an essentially premodern society, so they're likely to tend more toward the old fashioned &quot;property crime&quot; definition of rape: it's not so much about whether the victim consented as whether the victim's parents or spouse consented. I'm using gender neutral terms here, because gender privilege doesn't seem to be as big a deal for the Garou. It's more about whether you can Change, followed by whether you have Gnosis.<br /> <br /> And finally, accusations of cannibalism are about the oldest trick in the book on cultural chauvinism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for labelling Pentex bad guys, well, that one is pretty unambiguous. Pentex <i>are</i> bad guys, and they would be whether or not they served the Wyrm. Their entire market model is 'maximize human suffering', and not for a 'noble' purpose like 'human suffering purifies the soul' or 'suffering breaks the chains placed on us by the demiurge', but purely for 'it will make <i>us</i>, on the individual level, wealthier/happier/immortal/whatever-we-want, even if it makes the greater collective live in wretched misery'. The greedy, malevolent corporation that literally plans to enslave the totality of existence for its own benefit is evil in a way even the Dancers aren't. There's really no moral dilemma there - there might be on the individual employee level (Jim, the plant manager who unknowingly oversaw the introduction of tainted (just chemically, not with Banes) ingredients in baby formula - just for a random example - is not necessarily a bad person or an evil one. Killing him <i>is</i> a moral dilemma) but not on the corporate totality level. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Underpants Gnomes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Maximize human suffering<br /> 2. ?<br /> \u200b3. Profit!</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf has perfectly good banes and fomori if it wanted villains this simplistic. In the Black Spiral Dancers, there was potential for something much more interesting.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1087742#post1087742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's suspicious about it? In the same breath that one of the Garou or Fera realizes what they are, they also realize that the cosmos is dying. Then the Garou meets other Garou and finds out that their side is to blame for an awful lot of this shit, and they have mountains and valleys and oceans of work ahead if they're going to make anything right.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does &quot;the Weaver tried to bind the Wyrm in its pattern web and the Wyrm went insane&quot; actually mean? Does that even evoke a clear image for you? I don't see how it really explains anything. For starters, &quot;insane&quot; just isn't a very descriptive term at all. The entities involved feel more like abstract concepts or perhaps political factions than literal entities. It just doesn't strike me as interesting in itself, but it would make sense if it were a cover/abstraction for something far more complex.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not really a religion to them. It wouldn't be to humans, either, if they could see and freely communicate with spirits. </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's not a religion, it's a personal relationship with God!&quot;<br /> -- many Christians I've met in real life<br /> <br /> What you say definitely seems accurate when it comes to spirits from jagglings on up to anything you can take as a totem. But if you were born in the World of Darkness and didn't have access to the books, how would you verify that Gaia or the Triat literally existed? I feel like I would eventually have to resort to the same sorts of arguments that IRL theologians use, whether I was a werewolf or not. There's the old appeal to gnosis, except that the term and concept of &quot;gnosis&quot; was lifted directly from an IRL religion. You may have divine revelation, but claiming that you have divine revelation still doesn't set you apart from the religious.<br /> <br /> You can ask lesser spirits about their superiors, but then you run into what I call the &quot;you can't have your god and meet him, too&quot; problem. When the beings you call &quot;gods&quot; or &quot;spirits&quot; exist literally, and you can see, touch, and talk to them, and they have finite needs, resources, and motivations that can be threatened, not just in old stories, but before your eyes, your belief in them does cease to be religious. However, I would say that such a belief loses in gravitas what it gains in credibility. You're not talking about religion anymore, you're talking about interdimensional politics. The spirits you can actually meet in Werewolf are approximately as ephemeral and fallible as anyone else, so it's hard to say, as a werewolf, that their belief in Gaia and the Triat is any less faith-based than anyone else's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:27:23-07:00","id":1088056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1088031#post1088031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does &quot;the Weaver tried to bind the Wyrm in its pattern web and the Wyrm went insane&quot; actually mean? Does that even evoke a clear image for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>On some level, yes. A spider binding a snake in a web. A hand with scissors becoming hopelessly tangled in the threads that it seeks to cut. A balance scale tied so that it can't provide a meaningful form of its purpose. One divine being imprisoning the other, which happens a lot in various old tales. They're all pieces of the big picture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see how it really explains anything. For starters, &quot;insane&quot; just isn't a very descriptive term at all. The entities involved feel more like abstract concepts or perhaps political factions than literal entities. It just doesn't strike me as interesting in itself, but it would make sense if it were a cover/abstraction for something far more complex. </div> </div> </div>Descriptions of how and why the Weaver came to do what it did vary, but a more down to earth explanation is that it became like various iterations of Superman's foe Brainiac and sought to, essentially, know all and then make sure that its knowledge was perfect by making sure there wouldn't be anything new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;It's not a religion, it's a personal relationship with God!&quot;<br /> -- many Christians I've met in real life<br /> <br /> What you say definitely seems accurate when it comes to spirits from jagglings on up to anything you can take as a totem. But if you were born in the World of Darkness and didn't have access to the books, how would you verify that Gaia or the Triat literally existed? </div> </div> </div>Their frighteningly larger bits and pieces came to visit in the past, and were probably more accessible way further in the past. Recall, the Croatan had to sacrifice themselves to keep the Eater-of-Souls - a Celestine - from manifesting. Occasionally, you'll get more positive and uplifting visits from Gaian Celestine avatars, or extremely occasionally even an avatar of Gaia. Also, the Garou and Fera are really, really old. Like, they've had written language for tens of thousands of years longer than humans have, or in the case of Mokole, many tens of millions of years. Not all of the traditions are recited and memorized as epic poetry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like I would eventually have to resort to the same sorts of arguments that IRL theologians use, whether I was a werewolf or not. There's the old appeal to gnosis, except that the term and concept of &quot;gnosis&quot; was lifted directly from an IRL religion. You may have divine revelation, but claiming that you have divine revelation still doesn't set you apart from the religious. </div> </div> </div>Except that none of the Gnostics ever, to the best of anyone's knowledge, had to sacrifice themselves to keep a cosmic being's corrupt side from manifesting in the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can ask lesser spirits about their superiors, but then you run into what I call the &quot;you can't have your god and meet him, too&quot; problem. When the beings you call &quot;gods&quot; or &quot;spirits&quot; exist literally, and you can see, touch, and talk to them, and they have finite needs, resources, and motivations that can be threatened, not just in old stories, but before your eyes, your belief in them does cease to be religious. However, I would say that such a belief loses in gravitas what it gains in credibility. You're not talking about religion anymore, you're talking about interdimensional politics. The spirits you can actually meet in Werewolf are approximately as ephemeral and fallible as anyone else, so it's hard to say, as a werewolf, that their belief in Gaia and the Triat is any less faith-based than anyone else's. </div> </div> </div>Not really. Gnosis is the awareness of the cosmos as a whole. If you take Gaia as the whole, then the wider awareness is vaguely akin to cells in a body, only they have brains and think on their own. Some cells have turned against the body as a whole, while some still do what they need to do to keep the body from failing. They are distinct, yet all connected, and there are even some pieces that aren't necessarily of the whole's origin, but still part of it.<br /> <br /> As for fallibility, it gets weird. They don't exactly give you too many break points for what an Incarna can't process, seeing as how Incarnae and the beings above them don't have stats. They typically involve things on a Celestine's awareness. In their own domain and per their own purview, they aren't likely to fail, but the nature of spirits being what it is, what's outside that purview gets murkier. Fortunately, the Garou and Fera are in a position to take stock of what many different such spirits say to paint a more complete picture.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, Werewolf hasn't really dealt with existential crises of purpose, the power of belief, or lie-shrouded origins. That's for other games. Werewolf has always keen on having the setup be literally true and not second-guessing itself into pretzels of anxiety, theory, and internet flame wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:59:29-07:00","id":1088071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1088031#post1088031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so maybe this is on some level a conservative/liberal difference in readings? Because the &quot;Captain Planet&quot; thing was always the part I most sympathized with. It's impossible not to cherry-pick from canon, but over the years, a certain way of cherry-picking has become fan dogma.<br /> <br /> It's just that I haven't been able to enjoy the playstyles you mentioned when I'm expected to take all of the ridiculous sounding propaganda and superstition at face value for no good reason. &quot;Spiritually sterile&quot;? What does that even mean? Because all it sounds like is that there are religious taboos against circumventing metis sterility because it's a &quot;curse from Gaia&quot;, comparable to archaic Christian taboos against using medication to treat birthing pains. So not a lot of Garou have tried or reported the results. Except the Black Spiral Dancers, but everyone in the Garou Nation is prone to assuming those are all hideous Rosemary's babies of some kind. Not that they've ever, you know, met one, because eww. The First Litany and the rhetoric surrounding it sound too much like IRL homophobia for me to not want to explore that allegory.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sympathize because if you're playing a Garou, you've more than likely been indoctrinated to sympathize. Or you don't sympathize because you're a Bone Gnawer who studied philosophy and lives in a barrel and thinks it's all bullshit. Either way you can engage with the material, either unthinkingly or critically.<br /> <br /> Oh, and many Garou have met BSDs in the modern era. They aren't the boogeyman. They do exist, their existence is provable, and they interact - violently - with the greater community on a fairly regular existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know, I know, &quot;it's not like homosexuality, it's like incest&quot;. Except it's not quite directly analogous to either, and simplistic comparisons to incest are another common trope of anti-gay rhetoric. The incest comparison also seems like the pot calling the kettle a pervert, when it's coming from people who are as obsessed as the Garou are with breeding only with their kin for the sake of &quot;purity&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's the subtext, and yes, many fans for some reason don't quite grasp that the Garou are <i>terrible</i> at the litany and that the litany itself is a wee bit questionable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where I find the analogy between incest taboos and the first litany really collapses, though, is that most modern nations are not being torn apart by their incest taboos the way the Garou Nation is currently being torn apart by the First Litany. &quot;Think of the poor, deformed metis babies!&quot; and &quot;Love the metis, hate the parents!&quot; seem like sensible enough attitudes on the surface, and have more or less been adopted by most tribes. But if the Black Spiral Dancers' recruitment numbers are any indication, a whole lot of those &quot;pitiable, misbegotten creatures&quot; would much rather keep their deformities and not have their parents treated like shit. </div> </div> </div>This is literally a recurring plot point, and also a fairly natural consequence of deep ideological rifts in a society. To me, that's actually a plus - the Garou aren't necessarily nice guys, and having the areas that get all kinds of fucked up (like the murder of infants and their parents) be the source of deep conflict between tribes with different attitudes opens up a lot of potential for storytelling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, I keep asking simple questions like:<br /> <br /> How can the Black Spiral Dancers, as described, function as a tribe? </div> </div> </div>As described, fairly simply. They still have their tribal power structures, strengthened by ease of transit and communication. Most of their leaders aren't the 'screaming perma-rage berserker' or 'utterly incoherent lunatic' varieties that the tribe gets stereotyped as. They also have a trump card in the form of continual support from the Wyrm and its servants, further aiding them in reproduction, organization, and logistics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would anyone, in or out of their right mind, join the Black Spiral Dancers? </div> </div> </div>If you're a creature already filled with an unnatural rage that drives you into berserk furies who was in all likelihood raised or initiated into a death cult mindset, having the exact object of what you fight for shift a little isn't that unbelievable. Most BSDs are either born or raised into it, and those that defect or are captured and 'persuaded' to join do two things: Walk the Spiral - which is not just a generic 'save against insanity' but a progressive series of initiatory experiences at the hands of the Wyrm and its servants, revealing more and more of the mindset in gradual steps - and have a doubt in the first place to be exploited. Now when you consider that the Spiral's teachings aren't actually that crazy at the core (a lot of the rest is) since they want to restore the balance just like the other tribes and simply believe that the only way to do it is to burn it all down and start from scratch, it's even easier to see why people might join up even without the initiatory experience once they've lost all hope of restoration-without-destruction.<br /> <br /> Now add further that as of W20, their party line is 'the apocalypse already happened. All the Gaian Garou are doing is trying to protect a corpse, and prevent the natural cycle of birth-death-rebirth.'<br /> <br /> One might also ask why anyone would have hung out at the Abbey of Thelema...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How have the Black Spiral Dancers been able to not only continue existing, but become the biggest and fastest-growing tribe, in spite of being universally and relentlessly violent and nihilistic? </div> </div> </div>Black Spiral Dancers aren't in fact nihilistic. Their actions have a purpose and so do their lives. Mistaking 'the world is doomed, we need to end it/stop trying to keep it from disintegrating' - whether to be reborn anew or simply to end suffering - for nihilism is a big mistake and undermines the entire Spiral mindset and theology. Nor is the rejection of the Litany a nihilistic act, but rather one designed to shatter taboos that hold back the believer.<br /> <br /> So how can they be the fastest growing tribe? That's simple. They breed prolifically. They breed with whoever they like, because why wouldn't they? No part of their theology forbids it, no part of their struggle makes it unwise, and the experience is both pleasurable and satisfying. Some rape, others seduce, some just get drunk and see what happens. All is permissible, so why shouldn't they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But instead of answers, all I can find are what look like randomly selected passages from something H. R. Giger wrote when he was going through puberty. That's just bad storytelling. I can't find the verisimilitude in it. One could make an analogy to ISIL or something, but even ISIL has more coherent ideals and motivations than the Black Spiral Dancers. ISIL is also much smaller than many Muslim sects, whereas the Black Spiral Dancers are somehow the largest Garou tribe, and I don't think it's overly optimistic to say ISIL doesn't have much staying power. The Black Spiral Dancers have been around longer than Islam, IIRC. Groups like that have more going for them than orgies on speed.<br /> <br /> What I think makes more sense is to suppose that what we see of the Black Spiral Dancers is how the Garou Nation sees them, and how the Garou Nation sees them is similar to what people in countries with sharia law must envision when they hear about things like &quot;rape culture on American college campuses&quot;. The Garou Nation has such a reactionary and dogmatic view of sexuality that they can't picture a tribe that doesn't accept the First Litany as anything but a nonstop rape orgy. If one doesn't understand the social context, one pictures ritualistic gang rape, but the reality is usually a lot more mundane. </div> </div> </div>The majority is that way, or an attempt to 'out of universe' downplay the impact of the Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth. For a more understandable BSD tribe, read it with gnosticism on the mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, the Garou are an essentially premodern society, so they're likely to tend more toward the old fashioned &quot;property crime&quot; definition of rape: it's not so much about whether the victim consented as whether the victim's parents or spouse consented. I'm using gender neutral terms here, because gender privilege doesn't seem to be as big a deal for the Garou. It's more about whether you can Change, followed by whether you have Gnosis. </div> </div> </div>That depends on tribe, largely. It's an attitude you might find among some Fangs or Get or Fianna. It's not one you're likely to find among the Gnawers, Furies, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And finally, accusations of cannibalism are about the oldest trick in the book on cultural chauvinism. </div> </div> </div>Of course, they actually <i>are</i> cannibals by their own account. But so are a bunch of the Gaian tribes historically. For the Spirals, the eating of human flesh - as forbidden by the litany - is another of those taboos to break to achieve liberation from the old mindset.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf has perfectly good banes and fomori if it wanted villains this simplistic. In the Black Spiral Dancers, there was potential for something much more interesting. </div> </div> </div>And the Dancers are much more interesting. Pentex though is a 'simplistic' villain because corporate greed is a 'simplistic' evil. Remember, the two are different entities.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does &quot;the Weaver tried to bind the Wyrm in its pattern web and the Wyrm went insane&quot; actually mean? Does that even evoke a clear image for you? I don't see how it really explains anything. For starters, &quot;insane&quot; just isn't a very descriptive term at all. The entities involved feel more like abstract concepts or perhaps political factions than literal entities. It just doesn't strike me as interesting in itself, but it would make sense if it were a cover/abstraction for something far more complex. </div> </div> </div>It evokes a very clear image and I'm not sure why it doesn't for you. The entities <i>are</i> abstract concepts-turned-spirits, but that's far from uncommon in religion and the occult, but the underlying concept is simple. The principle of Ordering ('the Weaver'), finding the 'chaotic' entropy infesting its works, sought to prevent the destruction of its works. Unfortunately, without the constant cycle of birth-death-rebirth, all things fall apart, and that's exactly what happens next. 'The Wyrm', as that concept-spirit of entropic destruction and breakdown into raw elements, as the negrido, fragments and becomes unable to perform its task correctly.<br /> <br /> Everything else is a physical or spirit-physical (that is, 'physical' in the Umbra, not purely spiritual/intellectual) reflection of the higher spiritual dimensions where this plays out. Is there a literal spider weaving a dragon into its web? Yes, but that is only one reflection of the struggle between the two concept-deities. It's also the level that the lowly creatures born to the Lowest emanations can interact with, being incapable of interacting with the higher levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;It's not a religion, it's a personal relationship with God!&quot;<br /> -- many Christians I've met in real life<br /> <br /> What you say definitely seems accurate when it comes to spirits from jagglings on up to anything you can take as a totem. But if you were born in the World of Darkness and didn't have access to the books, how would you verify that Gaia or the Triat literally existed? I feel like I would eventually have to resort to the same sorts of arguments that IRL theologians use, whether I was a werewolf or not. There's the old appeal to gnosis, except that the term and concept of &quot;gnosis&quot; was lifted directly from an IRL religion. You may have divine revelation, but claiming that you have divine revelation still doesn't set you apart from the religious.<br /> <br /> You can ask lesser spirits about their superiors, but then you run into what I call the &quot;you can't have your god and meet him, too&quot; problem. When the beings you call &quot;gods&quot; or &quot;spirits&quot; exist literally, and you can see, touch, and talk to them, and they have finite needs, resources, and motivations that can be threatened, not just in old stories, but before your eyes, your belief in them does cease to be religious. However, I would say that such a belief loses in gravitas what it gains in credibility. You're not talking about religion anymore, you're talking about interdimensional politics. The spirits you can actually meet in Werewolf are approximately as ephemeral and fallible as anyone else, so it's hard to say, as a werewolf, that their belief in Gaia and the Triat is any less faith-based than anyone else's. </div> </div> </div>I dispute that meeting your gods makes them any less divine. It just means they don't fit quite into the Western conception of what a god is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T22:03:02-07:00","id":1088104,"title":"","content":"The Dancers point of View IS GIVEN <br /> <br /> 'Mwa Ha Ha Ha, I like to pollute, defile and corrupt!!!&quot; IS a viewpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T22:14:49-07:00","id":1088106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1088104#post1088104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dancers point of View IS GIVEN<br /> <br /> 'Mwa Ha Ha Ha, I like to pollute, defile and corrupt!!!&quot; IS a viewpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the annoying oversimplified view people trot out and which, unfortunately, is treated as the be all and end all too often both in discussions and in print. &quot;The world is broken; our job is to tear it down and/or kill its foolish defenders so that the big boss can eat it and shit it out as raw parts again.&quot; is much closer to the CoBL.<br /> <br /> Why pollute? Because it brings the end faster - and it breaks the Litany. Why defile? Because it brings the end faster - and it affirms devotion and liberates the defiler from Gaian morality. Why corrupt? Because it brings the end faster - and because it challenges the 'wisdom' of the Gaian philosophies. Why kill? Because it brings the end faster - and it is what the Garou were born to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:34:57-07:00","id":1088254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1088106#post1088106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the annoying oversimplified view people trot out and which, unfortunately, is treated as the be all and end all too often both in discussions and in print. &quot;The world is broken; our job is to tear it down and/or kill its foolish defenders so that the big boss can eat it and shit it out as raw parts again.&quot; is much closer to the CoBL.<br /> <br /> Why pollute? Because it brings the end faster - and it breaks the Litany. Why defile? Because it brings the end faster - and it affirms devotion and liberates the defiler from Gaian morality. Why corrupt? Because it brings the end faster - and because it challenges the 'wisdom' of the Gaian philosophies. Why kill? Because it brings the end faster - and it is what the Garou were born to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know all that, but was over simplifying on purpose..<br /> <br /> played in a white howler game at the grand masquerade that ended with...<br /> <br /> &quot;You realize the pointlessness that you cannot keep gaia from dieing forever, only prolong her suffering.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wanted him to know, that just because it doesnt help facilitate the kind of &quot;Shocking Reversal<span style=\"font-family:AppleSDGothicNeo-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2122 </span></span>&quot; He wanted, doesnt meant they arent given a viewpoint. &quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:19:21-07:00","id":1088298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1088106#post1088106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the annoying oversimplified view people trot out and which, unfortunately, is treated as the be all and end all too often both in discussions and in print. &quot;The world is broken; our job is to tear it down and/or kill its foolish defenders so that the big boss can eat it and shit it out as raw parts again.&quot; is much closer to the CoBL.<br /> <br /> Why pollute? Because it brings the end faster - and it breaks the Litany. Why defile? Because it brings the end faster - and it affirms devotion and liberates the defiler from Gaian morality. Why corrupt? Because it brings the end faster - and because it challenges the 'wisdom' of the Gaian philosophies. Why kill? Because it brings the end faster - and it is what the Garou were born to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's giving them a bit too much credit. W20 Book of the Wyrm flat out states that they're twisted and self-indulgent in their atrocities. The ones that can articulate the &quot;we already won!&quot; point of view coherently are just putting a gloss on something that they know in their heart isn't actually true (pg 117-118).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:39:21-07:00","id":1088339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1088298#post1088298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's giving them a bit too much credit. W20 Book of the Wyrm flat out states that they're twisted and self-indulgent in their atrocities. The ones that can articulate the &quot;we already won!&quot; point of view coherently are just putting a gloss on something that they know in their heart isn't actually true (pg 117-118).</div> </div> </div> </div>Psh, pro-Gaian propaganda! More seriously, you're right. It's part of what I referred to earlier with the attempt to downplay the CoBL, which is a direction I disagree with. Sadly though, I don't make the lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:25:21-07:00","id":1088363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1082476-destroying-the-garou-nation?p=1088106#post1088106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the annoying oversimplified view people trot out and which, unfortunately, is treated as the be all and end all too often both in discussions and in print. &quot;The world is broken; our job is to tear it down and/or kill its foolish defenders so that the big boss can eat it and shit it out as raw parts again.&quot; is much closer to the CoBL.<br /> <br /> Why pollute? Because it brings the end faster - and it breaks the Litany. Why defile? Because it brings the end faster - and it affirms devotion and liberates the defiler from Gaian morality. Why corrupt? Because it brings the end faster - and because it challenges the 'wisdom' of the Gaian philosophies. Why kill? Because it brings the end faster - and it is what the Garou were born to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, this is the interpretation of the BSD's that I like the most. They aren't just causing harm for the hell of it, they have an ideology and a sort of higher purpose which drives them to do what they do and, in some cases, justifies indulging in the worst aspect of the natures as they become increasingly spiritually tainted. I like the idea that a BSD might at some point sit down with you and make a case for why they're right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:36:10-07:00","id":1089212,"title":"","content":"Well, they might before you and your friends fill them full of silver for being Wyrm-twisted deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T18:11:46-07:00","id":1100665,"title":"","content":"I stole from Forsaken in my game and the Garou Nation has split between the Pure and the Modern. The Garou Nation didn't split on a tribal level but has done on a much messier Camarilla vs. Sabbat level. The Red Talons went almost 100% Pure while the Bone Gnawers went almost 100% Modern. The Silver Fangs mostly went Pure while the Shadow Lords mostly went Modern.<br /> <br /> It's been working well so far.<br /> <br /> Re: Black Spiral Dancers<br /> <br /> I don't think that many Black Spiral Dancers have that much coherence left to talk about their philosophy. Weirdly, if you want to talk to a Garou about the Wyrm being redeemed and why the universe should be destroyed, you're probably better off talking to some really extremist Uktena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}